1
00:00:03,040 --> 00:00:08,039
You know what you did today was basically
announcing to the whole school that

2
00:00:08,119 --> 00:00:09,760
you're officially one of Toxxxxin, right?

3
00:00:09,840 --> 00:00:11,240
I wanted it that way.

4
00:00:11,320 --> 00:00:14,320
<i>I know being here might mean facing things</i>
<i>I never expected.</i>

5
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:16,520
<i>But I've made up my mind.</i>

6
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:17,960
<i>I'm staying right here</i>

7
00:00:18,040 --> 00:00:19,560
<i>because I really like being here.</i>

8
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:24,440
<i>I really do.</i>

9
00:00:29,240 --> 00:00:35,040
<i>Honestly, if you ask me where</i>
<i>Project Renew Junjai is supposed to end,</i>

10
00:00:35,120 --> 00:00:36,840
<i>it's still kind of fuzzy.</i>

11
00:00:37,680 --> 00:00:41,200
<i>I know things have to change,</i>
<i>but how much?</i>

12
00:00:41,280 --> 00:00:42,600
<i>Will I really stop getting bullied?</i>

13
00:00:42,680 --> 00:00:43,520
Let's go home.

14
00:00:43,600 --> 00:00:45,880
<i>Nobody seems to have an answer yet.</i>

15
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:47,480
Bye.

16
00:00:47,560 --> 00:00:51,920
<i>In the end, Aidao told me</i>
<i>to keep things as they are for now.</i>

17
00:00:53,720 --> 00:00:55,080
<i>Pretty vague, right?</i>

18
00:00:55,840 --> 00:01:00,000
<i>But I guess being a teenager means</i>
<i>dealing with a lot of stuff like that.</i>

19
00:01:01,280 --> 00:01:03,840
<i>Oh, but one thing I know for sure</i>

20
00:01:04,640 --> 00:01:07,000
<i>is that Aidao's still having that dream.</i>

21
00:01:09,400 --> 00:01:10,880
<i>And the more she has it,</i>

22
00:01:11,760 --> 00:01:14,320
<i>the harder it is for her to stop smiling.</i>

23
00:01:16,600 --> 00:01:17,520
<i>Cute, right?</i>

24
00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:21,000
Having a good dream, were you?

25
00:01:21,760 --> 00:01:24,440
Uncle Jess! How'd you get into my room?

26
00:01:24,520 --> 00:01:28,120
I came to get the shirts you borrowed
for that Sports Day shoot or whatever.

27
00:01:28,200 --> 00:01:29,920
You never gave them back.

28
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:31,600
You didn't even tell me
who you gave them to.

29
00:01:31,680 --> 00:01:35,240
My niece is so secretive.

30
00:01:35,320 --> 00:01:37,720
Or was it this girl from the news?

31
00:01:40,160 --> 00:01:42,120
GOLD MEDALIST CAUSES STIR
ATTENDS EXAM OUT OF UNIFORM

32
00:01:42,720 --> 00:01:44,520
She looks promising, though.

33
00:01:44,600 --> 00:01:47,080
Uncle Jess, that iPad's mine!

34
00:01:47,160 --> 00:01:51,080
Then why did you give me the password?
Who watches news like this before bed?

35
00:01:51,160 --> 00:01:52,720
I'm someone who loves learning.

36
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:55,480
What's so weird about
keeping up with school news?

37
00:01:55,560 --> 00:01:57,120
Here you go. Here. Here.

38
00:01:57,200 --> 00:01:58,960
You can go now.

39
00:01:59,040 --> 00:02:00,160
Thanks.

40
00:02:01,520 --> 00:02:05,720
I mean it. I really like it
when you make that face.

41
00:02:07,360 --> 00:02:08,600
What face?

42
00:02:09,800 --> 00:02:12,240
The face you make
when you're in love, I guess.

43
00:02:20,640 --> 00:02:22,520
The face I make when I'm in love?

44
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:24,680
Damn. What kind of face is that?

45
00:02:27,840 --> 00:02:29,360
Do I look normal yet?

46
00:02:35,360 --> 00:02:38,200
Aww, that's nice!

47
00:02:38,280 --> 00:02:40,400
All that care I put into raising you
was worth it.

48
00:02:41,280 --> 00:02:42,240
Great job!

49
00:02:42,880 --> 00:02:44,120
What's with you guys?

50
00:02:44,200 --> 00:02:46,720
Here she comes. Go ahead and tell her.

51
00:02:52,280 --> 00:02:55,440
So, a modeling agency just called.

52
00:02:56,640 --> 00:03:01,920
They want to sign me.

53
00:03:04,040 --> 00:03:05,000
JUNJAI LOOKS LIKE A MODEL

54
00:03:08,480 --> 00:03:12,240
Girl, Junjai is going to be
a professional model!

55
00:03:14,200 --> 00:03:17,040
Wait. What's with that face?

56
00:03:17,680 --> 00:03:19,480
What? What face am I making? Nothing!

57
00:03:19,560 --> 00:03:22,560
- Stop! Don't look.
- Don't look.

58
00:03:22,640 --> 00:03:23,560
Stop!

59
00:03:23,640 --> 00:03:24,840
Don't look. Don't look!

60
00:04:04,680 --> 00:04:05,920
Excited!

61
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:08,160
Here you are. A name card.
I've prepared it for you.

62
00:04:08,240 --> 00:04:09,480
Here's your blazer!

63
00:04:09,560 --> 00:04:10,600
A cap and sunglasses too.

64
00:04:10,680 --> 00:04:13,400
Do you guys have to be this serious?

65
00:04:13,480 --> 00:04:16,440
Of course. You're about
to make your debut.

66
00:04:16,519 --> 00:04:18,320
<i>You have to make</i>
<i>a killer first impression.</i>

67
00:04:18,399 --> 00:04:20,519
<i>Both the model and her managers!</i>

68
00:04:20,600 --> 00:04:21,959
Ask Aidao if you don't believe me.

69
00:04:25,800 --> 00:04:26,640
Yeah.

70
00:04:28,120 --> 00:04:29,200
Right.

71
00:04:30,600 --> 00:04:32,080
I think we should just leave her alone.

72
00:04:32,160 --> 00:04:33,240
Seriously.

73
00:04:33,320 --> 00:04:36,480
If you're not okay with it,

74
00:04:36,560 --> 00:04:37,840
we can go down on our own.

75
00:04:37,920 --> 00:04:40,160
No, no. I'm okay.

76
00:04:41,600 --> 00:04:43,120
Okay, if you say so.

77
00:04:56,120 --> 00:04:57,000
What about you, though?

78
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:01,600
We never actually asked
if you wanted to be a model, did we?

79
00:05:04,240 --> 00:05:06,360
You can tell us if you don't want to.

80
00:05:06,440 --> 00:05:08,920
I wouldn't say I don't want to.

81
00:05:10,440 --> 00:05:12,720
I'm just a little confused.

82
00:05:16,760 --> 00:05:22,000
Well, I don't even know
what being a model involves.

83
00:05:24,760 --> 00:05:28,280
<i>It's always felt a million miles away</i>
<i>from my life.</i>

84
00:05:29,880 --> 00:05:34,240
<i>Seeing all those pretty people</i>
<i>in pretty outfits…</i>

85
00:05:34,320 --> 00:05:37,280
<i>It's like a whole other world.</i>

86
00:05:38,960 --> 00:05:45,200
So I'm still figuring out
how to feel about it.

87
00:05:51,840 --> 00:05:55,960
Then take your time and learn.

88
00:05:57,720 --> 00:05:59,160
Don't worry.

89
00:05:59,240 --> 00:06:01,000
You're with Toxxxxxin.

90
00:06:05,400 --> 00:06:08,640
Leave the hard stuff to us.

91
00:06:15,040 --> 00:06:18,160
MODEL MANAGEMENT AGREEMENT
TERMS AND CONDITIONS

92
00:06:18,920 --> 00:06:21,480
Guys, are contracts usually this long?

93
00:06:22,400 --> 00:06:23,480
Hang on.

94
00:06:23,560 --> 00:06:27,280
So everyone in this group is her manager?

95
00:06:28,240 --> 00:06:29,080
Yes.

96
00:06:29,160 --> 00:06:30,360
That's adorable.

97
00:06:30,440 --> 00:06:32,440
I'm Bazu.

98
00:06:34,120 --> 00:06:35,000
Tell you what.

99
00:06:35,080 --> 00:06:38,200
Do you want to come upstairs
and see my agency?

100
00:06:41,080 --> 00:06:43,000
Come on, make yourselves at home.
Come, come, come.

101
00:06:43,080 --> 00:06:43,920
Let's go.

102
00:06:44,520 --> 00:06:46,200
Don't worry. Come right up.

103
00:06:46,280 --> 00:06:47,480
This way.

104
00:06:48,160 --> 00:06:51,160
My agency might be small,

105
00:06:51,240 --> 00:06:55,080
and we don't have many models yet,
but we're growing.

106
00:06:55,160 --> 00:06:57,960
I turned this area into a little studio.

107
00:06:58,040 --> 00:07:01,600
When clients come in for a shoot,
we do it right here.

108
00:07:01,680 --> 00:07:05,760
For hair and makeup, we go downstairs.

109
00:07:05,840 --> 00:07:10,240
Most of your first jobs
would be right here, Junjai.

110
00:07:10,320 --> 00:07:14,200
That is, if you decide to sign with me.

111
00:07:14,800 --> 00:07:18,240
Well, can I ask you something?

112
00:07:18,320 --> 00:07:20,280
How did you find Junjai?

113
00:07:20,360 --> 00:07:23,520
That viral clip
from the math competition she entered.

114
00:07:23,600 --> 00:07:26,760
Do you know how much buzz it got online?

115
00:07:28,120 --> 00:07:29,120
Is that really all?

116
00:07:29,200 --> 00:07:30,800
Lots of people in this industry

117
00:07:30,880 --> 00:07:33,480
get their start
with something small like that.

118
00:07:36,040 --> 00:07:39,800
I know you're worried
I might be a scammer.

119
00:07:39,880 --> 00:07:41,200
But trust me.

120
00:07:41,280 --> 00:07:46,520
If I get to take care of Junjai,
I'll do everything I can to help her grow.

121
00:08:00,720 --> 00:08:02,280
Hey, watch out for the flash!

122
00:08:03,840 --> 00:08:05,960
Ow! Does it sting?

123
00:08:07,920 --> 00:08:09,800
So, what do you say?

124
00:08:12,720 --> 00:08:13,920
Bazu.

125
00:08:17,200 --> 00:08:20,640
Do you really think someone like me
could be a model?

126
00:08:22,920 --> 00:08:25,520
My agency might be small,
but I've got an eye for talent.

127
00:08:25,600 --> 00:08:27,320
I've never been wrong.

128
00:08:35,320 --> 00:08:37,039
- IS THIS AGENCY ANY GOOD?
- UNCLE JESS: YEAH.

129
00:08:37,120 --> 00:08:39,280
I WORK WITH THEM ALL THE TIME.
CONFIRMED.

130
00:08:43,480 --> 00:08:46,520
In that case, I'll sign.

131
00:08:48,160 --> 00:08:50,920
- Sign now!
- Yes, sign.

132
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:52,400
JUNJAI JANYAKUL

133
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:55,840
Hey, wait, wait. Hold on.

134
00:08:56,960 --> 00:08:58,040
- Yes?
- Is something wrong?

135
00:08:58,120 --> 00:08:59,320
Let me see that.

136
00:09:00,160 --> 00:09:01,160
Hey!

137
00:09:02,560 --> 00:09:03,640
Oh no.

138
00:09:04,280 --> 00:09:06,920
You girls go to Saint Cecilia?

139
00:09:08,840 --> 00:09:11,360
Oh, I'm so sorry.

140
00:09:11,440 --> 00:09:15,120
I didn't know you went to that school.

141
00:09:15,720 --> 00:09:17,160
Is that a problem?

142
00:09:20,160 --> 00:09:24,680
You girls really don't know?
Your school's on a whole other level.

143
00:09:27,040 --> 00:09:30,200
Why the hell didn't I ask
where you went to school?

144
00:09:41,680 --> 00:09:43,000
What's up with you guys?

145
00:09:43,080 --> 00:09:44,240
Did you find it?

146
00:09:44,320 --> 00:09:45,520
Here it is. Found it.

147
00:09:47,360 --> 00:09:48,760
Holy shit, it's real.

148
00:09:48,840 --> 00:09:50,120
Let's go see Ms. Nicha.

149
00:09:58,040 --> 00:09:59,000
What?

150
00:10:01,120 --> 00:10:01,960
Yes.

151
00:10:03,520 --> 00:10:05,440
The school doesn't allow students

152
00:10:05,520 --> 00:10:08,440
to take on any kind
of commercial performance work.

153
00:10:08,520 --> 00:10:13,840
That includes films, television dramas,
and modeling of any kind.

154
00:10:14,680 --> 00:10:17,320
Last year, a student took a job
without telling the school.

155
00:10:18,520 --> 00:10:20,440
They were severely punished.

156
00:10:21,080 --> 00:10:23,440
Eh? What the heck?

157
00:10:23,520 --> 00:10:26,920
You girls mustn't go behind
the school's back, either.

158
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:29,200
You won't be able to keep it from them.

159
00:10:30,520 --> 00:10:31,560
But Ms. Nicha,

160
00:10:31,640 --> 00:10:34,400
can't we do anything about this rule?

161
00:10:34,480 --> 00:10:38,360
You can see
it's total bullshit too, can't you?

162
00:10:38,440 --> 00:10:41,440
Exactly. Does being a model
make you dumber?

163
00:10:42,160 --> 00:10:43,080
That's ridiculous.

164
00:10:43,160 --> 00:10:45,000
But rules are rules.

165
00:10:45,080 --> 00:10:47,440
My job is to enforce them.

166
00:10:47,520 --> 00:10:50,560
I can't go breaking them, can I?

167
00:10:57,480 --> 00:10:58,560
Anyway,

168
00:10:58,640 --> 00:11:04,000
luckily, the school does allow

169
00:11:04,080 --> 00:11:05,960
one exception.

170
00:11:06,520 --> 00:11:09,280
If you talk
to the student council president

171
00:11:09,920 --> 00:11:13,280
and get signatures
from more than 70% of the students,

172
00:11:13,360 --> 00:11:15,800
the president can submit a proposal
on your behalf.

173
00:11:15,880 --> 00:11:18,240
Whatever rule it is,

174
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:23,400
the school will accept
the proposal for discussion.

175
00:11:24,960 --> 00:11:27,280
If you can do that, I can help.

176
00:11:27,360 --> 00:11:28,920
Really?

177
00:11:31,600 --> 00:11:33,160
But the tricky part is that

178
00:11:33,800 --> 00:11:37,240
the previous president's term just ended.

179
00:11:37,320 --> 00:11:40,400
If you want to submit a proposal,

180
00:11:40,480 --> 00:11:44,840
you'll have to talk to the new candidate.

181
00:11:44,920 --> 00:11:47,800
Well, that doesn't sound too hard.

182
00:11:53,760 --> 00:11:54,640
Wait.

183
00:11:55,560 --> 00:12:02,120
Who's running
for student council president?

184
00:12:04,040 --> 00:12:05,240
Come on, everyone!

185
00:12:05,320 --> 00:12:08,000
Let's make our school
a better place together.

186
00:12:08,080 --> 00:12:10,200
Vote Ploypim, number one!

187
00:12:10,280 --> 00:12:11,840
Number one!

188
00:12:11,920 --> 00:12:15,400
If you're passing by, feel free to stop
and check out our policies.

189
00:12:15,480 --> 00:12:16,680
We're screwed.

190
00:12:23,400 --> 00:12:30,080
Sorry, but changing school rules
isn't part of our policy right now,

191
00:12:31,120 --> 00:12:33,960
especially when it comes to working
in entertainment.

192
00:12:34,040 --> 00:12:35,480
I'm totally against it.

193
00:12:36,480 --> 00:12:41,640
But changing this rule would open up
opportunities for every student.

194
00:12:41,720 --> 00:12:43,320
Every student?

195
00:12:44,880 --> 00:12:45,720
How, exactly?

196
00:12:46,520 --> 00:12:49,600
You're obviously doing this
for one student.

197
00:12:49,680 --> 00:12:53,240
If you're going to change a school rule,
it should benefit everyone, right?

198
00:12:53,320 --> 00:12:56,400
Why should the elite get
whatever they want

199
00:12:57,320 --> 00:12:59,080
just because they asked?

200
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:01,120
Right?

201
00:13:03,240 --> 00:13:05,840
I think you'd better find another way.

202
00:13:05,920 --> 00:13:07,720
I'm not changing it.

203
00:13:13,640 --> 00:13:16,520
How did Ploypim even get to run
for student council in the first place?

204
00:13:17,160 --> 00:13:18,440
Isn't she only in Grade 11?

205
00:13:18,520 --> 00:13:20,200
There's no rule against it.

206
00:13:21,160 --> 00:13:23,600
Her dad's the head
of the parents' association,

207
00:13:23,680 --> 00:13:25,080
and they're close to the principal.

208
00:13:25,800 --> 00:13:26,960
She's one of the elite herself,

209
00:13:27,040 --> 00:13:29,360
and she still has the nerve
to call other people out.

210
00:13:29,440 --> 00:13:32,600
So we're out of options, right?

211
00:13:34,040 --> 00:13:34,880
No.

212
00:13:35,480 --> 00:13:37,560
I'll try talking to the principal again.

213
00:13:37,640 --> 00:13:40,560
If they let us
collect signatures on our own,

214
00:13:40,640 --> 00:13:41,920
we still have a shot.

215
00:13:42,520 --> 00:13:44,080
Come on, Chelsea. Let's go.

216
00:13:44,920 --> 00:13:46,640
Hey, I'm coming too.

217
00:13:46,720 --> 00:13:49,280
I think just the two of us
should talk to the principal.

218
00:13:49,960 --> 00:13:51,280
You two wait here, okay?

219
00:13:52,120 --> 00:13:53,880
And don't start anything, Meimei.

220
00:13:54,760 --> 00:13:56,920
This is sensitive, okay?

221
00:14:03,880 --> 00:14:05,560
Okay. All right, let's…

222
00:14:05,640 --> 00:14:07,520
I've figured out what to do!

223
00:14:08,760 --> 00:14:11,520
But Chelsea said…

224
00:14:11,600 --> 00:14:13,160
Don't worry.

225
00:14:13,240 --> 00:14:17,680
It's just a regular campaign.

226
00:14:19,240 --> 00:14:20,880
There won't be anything strange about it.

227
00:14:41,920 --> 00:14:45,120
CHOOSE A PARTY WILLING TO CHANGE
THE SCHOOL RULES

228
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:46,880
Everyone!

229
00:14:46,960 --> 00:14:49,400
Does everyone want to fix
our school's rules?

230
00:14:49,480 --> 00:14:50,560
<i>Grab it and read.</i>

231
00:14:50,640 --> 00:14:52,480
These dinosaur-era rules have to change!

232
00:14:52,560 --> 00:14:55,240
So this isn't weird?

233
00:14:56,080 --> 00:14:58,880
She can do more than this, trust me.

234
00:15:05,520 --> 00:15:07,240
Let's help!

235
00:15:07,800 --> 00:15:09,480
Grab it and read!

236
00:15:09,560 --> 00:15:11,160
Please support it.

237
00:15:11,240 --> 00:15:13,040
I hope a lot of you support it.

238
00:15:14,320 --> 00:15:16,440
I understand, but we really can't fix it.

239
00:15:16,520 --> 00:15:18,920
Rules are rules. They can't be changed.

240
00:15:21,040 --> 00:15:24,240
Principal, here's what we'll do.
We'll collect the signatures ourselves.

241
00:15:25,160 --> 00:15:26,200
Forget it.

242
00:15:26,280 --> 00:15:27,640
This is all they can do.

243
00:15:30,760 --> 00:15:32,760
THIS PARTY DOESN'T WANT TO CHANGE.

244
00:15:34,960 --> 00:15:36,160
MEIMEI IS SO MISCHIEVOUS!

245
00:15:36,240 --> 00:15:40,840
<i>Do you ever feel like our school</i>
<i>is full of ridiculous rules?</i>

246
00:15:40,920 --> 00:15:43,960
<i>Let's campaign to get rid of these rules.</i>

247
00:15:44,840 --> 00:15:47,320
<i>Let's change things for a better future</i>
<i>at our own school.</i>

248
00:15:47,400 --> 00:15:50,360
- Why are you being so loud?!
- Please check it out.

249
00:15:51,680 --> 00:15:54,040
You've got some pretty amazing friends.

250
00:15:56,560 --> 00:15:59,720
But the school doesn't allow littering.

251
00:15:59,800 --> 00:16:02,560
Tell your seniors
to come pick all of this up.

252
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:06,680
I'm sorry.

253
00:16:07,520 --> 00:16:10,440
If you want to hand out flyers,
hand them out properly.

254
00:16:10,520 --> 00:16:12,680
They shouldn't end up all over the ground.

255
00:16:14,640 --> 00:16:16,400
Thank you, Ms. Nicha.

256
00:16:17,960 --> 00:16:22,080
It's about time
we changed our school's outdated rules.

257
00:16:22,160 --> 00:16:24,880
We should have more freedom at school.

258
00:16:24,960 --> 00:16:26,040
So we're counting on you.

259
00:16:26,120 --> 00:16:29,840
If you want to change these dinosaur-era
rules, come sign the petition.

260
00:16:29,920 --> 00:16:31,320
Bye-bye.

261
00:16:32,120 --> 00:16:36,160
By the way, what number
are Toxxxxxin running under?

262
00:16:36,960 --> 00:16:38,480
Oh, we're not running.

263
00:16:38,560 --> 00:16:40,840
We're just campaigning for this.

264
00:16:44,440 --> 00:16:47,000
They really can't
get those signatures, right?

265
00:16:47,080 --> 00:16:48,320
That's frustrating.

266
00:16:57,480 --> 00:17:00,800
Hey, aren't you even going to help?

267
00:17:00,880 --> 00:17:02,720
I'm exhausted, okay?

268
00:17:02,800 --> 00:17:04,200
I've already done plenty.

269
00:17:12,079 --> 00:17:14,520
You still don't trust her?

270
00:17:16,079 --> 00:17:17,160
It's not quite that.

271
00:17:17,240 --> 00:17:19,720
I just want to know

272
00:17:19,800 --> 00:17:21,839
if what we're doing

273
00:17:22,640 --> 00:17:25,839
is actually what Aidao saw in her dream.

274
00:17:29,440 --> 00:17:30,360
I don't know.

275
00:17:34,280 --> 00:17:36,880
I have no idea
what Aidao's thinking right now.

276
00:17:37,680 --> 00:17:40,920
And I understand Junjai even less.

277
00:17:42,600 --> 00:17:47,440
Maybe we should give them both
time to figure out…

278
00:17:49,360 --> 00:17:51,320
<i>what they actually want.</i>

279
00:17:52,800 --> 00:17:55,400
<i>Because if we keep going at this blindly,</i>

280
00:17:56,200 --> 00:17:57,320
<i>then you know</i>

281
00:17:58,720 --> 00:18:01,040
that nothing's going to change
in the end, right?

282
00:18:08,480 --> 00:18:11,000
<i>See? Ten minutes handing out flyers.</i>

283
00:18:11,080 --> 00:18:12,880
<i>Three hours picking up trash.</i>

284
00:18:12,960 --> 00:18:14,600
<i>So worth it.</i>

285
00:18:14,680 --> 00:18:17,720
<i>The principal won't yield,</i>
<i>and Ploypim's making things even worse.</i>

286
00:18:18,920 --> 00:18:20,160
<i>Did you see what she posted?</i>

287
00:18:20,240 --> 00:18:22,200
OUR PARTY WON'T CHANGE THE RULES.

288
00:18:23,360 --> 00:18:25,720
Yeah, I saw it.

289
00:18:26,520 --> 00:18:30,280
Hey, what if we back
one of the other candidates?

290
00:18:31,120 --> 00:18:32,760
<i>We've got even less of a chance with them.</i>

291
00:18:32,840 --> 00:18:34,680
I bet people don't even know their names.

292
00:18:34,760 --> 00:18:38,120
Meimei screwed this up.
I'm going to yell at her tomorrow.

293
00:18:38,200 --> 00:18:39,640
<i>Come on.</i>

294
00:18:39,720 --> 00:18:42,960
She's just trying to help in her own way.

295
00:18:43,880 --> 00:18:46,760
<i>Yeah. You love your friend, huh?</i>
<i>You love your friend so much.</i>

296
00:18:47,480 --> 00:18:48,920
Come on.

297
00:18:50,240 --> 00:18:52,640
Not as much as someone, I guess.

298
00:18:52,720 --> 00:18:54,440
What? Watch it!

299
00:19:02,360 --> 00:19:03,360
Hey.

300
00:19:04,520 --> 00:19:08,200
<i>You know that even if we can't change</i>
<i>the school rule today,</i>

301
00:19:08,280 --> 00:19:12,480
<i>Junjai can still model</i>
<i>once she graduates, right?</i>

302
00:19:14,480 --> 00:19:17,160
<i>At this point, I'm done asking</i>

303
00:19:17,240 --> 00:19:19,560
<i>whether it matches</i>
<i>what you saw in your dream.</i>

304
00:19:20,800 --> 00:19:22,800
<i>- But I think--</i>
- No.

305
00:19:23,440 --> 00:19:26,680
It really doesn't match.

306
00:19:28,960 --> 00:19:30,160
Not even close.

307
00:19:33,640 --> 00:19:36,160
<i>Sometimes I wonder</i>

308
00:19:36,920 --> 00:19:38,880
what the heck we're even doing.

309
00:19:43,240 --> 00:19:48,760
But when we went to the agency today,

310
00:19:50,320 --> 00:19:52,520
there was a moment,

311
00:19:52,600 --> 00:19:56,240
just a split second…

312
00:19:59,040 --> 00:20:01,160
when Junjai looked me in the eye.

313
00:20:01,240 --> 00:20:03,040
Hey, watch out for the flash!

314
00:20:03,120 --> 00:20:04,960
Ow! That stings?

315
00:20:13,320 --> 00:20:18,920
It was like another image overlapped
with what I was seeing.

316
00:20:24,240 --> 00:20:25,960
<i>It still didn't look the same at all,</i>

317
00:20:26,600 --> 00:20:29,360
<i>but I could feel</i>

318
00:20:30,440 --> 00:20:32,520
how close it was.

319
00:20:34,040 --> 00:20:35,680
That's abstract as hell.

320
00:20:36,840 --> 00:20:37,880
I'm sorry.

321
00:20:39,400 --> 00:20:42,160
Shit, I've wasted so much of your time.

322
00:20:45,720 --> 00:20:47,000
Come on.

323
00:20:47,080 --> 00:20:50,040
That's love. It's abstract.

324
00:20:52,280 --> 00:20:53,160
Hey.

325
00:20:53,240 --> 00:20:54,680
<i>We're even.</i>

326
00:21:01,000 --> 00:21:02,040
Aidao.

327
00:21:03,760 --> 00:21:06,920
<i>Deep down, you know</i>

328
00:21:08,080 --> 00:21:10,280
<i>there's still one other way, right?</i>

329
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:13,400
Stop. Don't even say it.

330
00:21:14,480 --> 00:21:16,640
<i>Just thinking about it</i>
<i>gives me goosebumps.</i>

331
00:21:16,720 --> 00:21:18,600
<i>Your dad will come after you</i>
<i>if you do that.</i>

332
00:21:18,680 --> 00:21:21,480
Yeah. My dad would kill me for sure.

333
00:21:21,560 --> 00:21:22,800
Then don't do it.

334
00:21:24,720 --> 00:21:26,200
Hey, Dim!

335
00:21:26,280 --> 00:21:29,960
Why does everyone
keep barging in without a word?

336
00:21:31,160 --> 00:21:33,280
This is a girl's room!

337
00:21:42,280 --> 00:21:46,120
Aidao, Dad wants to talk to us.

338
00:22:43,280 --> 00:22:46,560
Did something happen to you?

339
00:22:49,360 --> 00:22:50,400
Yeah, something happened.

340
00:22:52,720 --> 00:22:54,400
Was it that bad?

341
00:23:00,760 --> 00:23:04,040
You can tell me if you want.

342
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:08,240
I'd like to listen.

343
00:23:12,360 --> 00:23:14,040
<i>Do you know why I called you in?</i>

344
00:23:20,240 --> 00:23:21,200
No, Dad.

345
00:23:29,560 --> 00:23:31,560
It's about the paper
you had your sister help you with.

346
00:23:38,840 --> 00:23:39,920
You did very well.

347
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:47,480
You did whatever it took
to get the result I asked for.

348
00:23:48,200 --> 00:23:50,280
And when you use family,

349
00:23:50,920 --> 00:23:54,040
you can be sure the secret won't get out.

350
00:23:54,120 --> 00:23:55,960
You've grown up.

351
00:23:56,040 --> 00:23:57,240
Thank you.

352
00:23:59,800 --> 00:24:01,360
Unlike Aidao.

353
00:24:11,880 --> 00:24:13,560
You keep getting into more fights.

354
00:24:14,360 --> 00:24:16,200
Running wild with your friends.

355
00:24:16,280 --> 00:24:19,160
Ganging up on a younger student at school.

356
00:24:19,800 --> 00:24:24,840
Did you really think
that family let it go because of you?

357
00:24:33,520 --> 00:24:35,480
You knew about it too, didn't you?

358
00:24:36,440 --> 00:24:37,720
Yes, Dad.

359
00:24:40,360 --> 00:24:41,840
Why didn't you stop her?

360
00:24:41,920 --> 00:24:43,800
And you went and backed her up?
What were you doing?

361
00:24:44,960 --> 00:24:46,320
Huh? Get up!

362
00:24:48,880 --> 00:24:50,440
Remember what I taught you?

363
00:24:50,520 --> 00:24:53,360
If one Laosathitphong gets into trouble,

364
00:24:53,440 --> 00:24:54,760
it affects the whole family.

365
00:24:58,120 --> 00:25:01,880
From now on, neither of you can afford
to act this stupid.

366
00:25:01,960 --> 00:25:03,240
Understand?

367
00:25:04,080 --> 00:25:05,160
- Yes.
- Yes.

368
00:25:07,400 --> 00:25:09,640
- Do you understand?!
- Yes, Dad!

369
00:25:14,080 --> 00:25:15,000
Good.

370
00:25:22,440 --> 00:25:24,120
Come on. Both of you.

371
00:25:24,200 --> 00:25:25,400
Come.

372
00:25:28,080 --> 00:25:30,040
I love you both very much.

373
00:25:33,000 --> 00:25:34,040
Hey.

374
00:25:35,600 --> 00:25:39,520
You used to have strange dreams as a kid.
Do you still have that condition?

375
00:25:43,520 --> 00:25:44,400
Not anymore.

376
00:25:45,360 --> 00:25:46,200
Good.

377
00:25:46,840 --> 00:25:47,720
Remember this.

378
00:25:49,360 --> 00:25:54,560
Those pointless dreams
will only keep you from growing up.

379
00:26:12,240 --> 00:26:13,360
I'm sorry.

380
00:26:15,640 --> 00:26:19,960
I really can't talk about this.

381
00:26:25,360 --> 00:26:30,000
Then can I just sit here quietly with you?

382
00:26:55,160 --> 00:26:59,080
Have you ever heard
that thing about doors?

383
00:27:05,920 --> 00:27:07,840
It's said

384
00:27:09,440 --> 00:27:15,000
your future is like
a bunch of doors in front of you.

385
00:27:17,800 --> 00:27:19,240
<i>They wait for you to open them.</i>

386
00:27:21,440 --> 00:27:27,920
<i>People always tell me how lucky I am.</i>

387
00:27:29,560 --> 00:27:31,680
That I've got more opportunities
than anyone else.

388
00:27:32,680 --> 00:27:35,320
Like I can open any door I want.

389
00:27:37,840 --> 00:27:39,280
<i>But I feel like</i>

390
00:27:40,480 --> 00:27:45,080
<i>every single door is closed to me.</i>

391
00:27:48,160 --> 00:27:51,400
<i>And the more opportunities I seem to have,</i>

392
00:27:53,360 --> 00:27:54,840
<i>the more I realize…</i>

393
00:27:58,120 --> 00:28:00,160
I can't actually do anything.

394
00:28:09,000 --> 00:28:11,720
I can't even help you become a model.

395
00:28:18,200 --> 00:28:24,560
I'm sorry I dragged you into all this

396
00:28:26,480 --> 00:28:28,880
when you never asked for any of it.

397
00:28:30,720 --> 00:28:35,400
I've been so damn selfish.

398
00:28:56,440 --> 00:28:57,480
You know what?

399
00:28:57,560 --> 00:28:59,920
My aunt once told me something.

400
00:29:00,000 --> 00:29:04,520
When we're stressed, it's because
the voices in our heads get too loud.

401
00:29:06,560 --> 00:29:07,640
So?

402
00:29:08,480 --> 00:29:11,520
So right now,
you need to blast some music.

403
00:29:13,920 --> 00:29:15,000
Put it on.

404
00:29:15,760 --> 00:29:18,520
And shake it all out of your head!

405
00:29:23,040 --> 00:29:24,000
Come on!

406
00:29:26,200 --> 00:29:28,760
Hey, isn't that too loud?

407
00:29:28,840 --> 00:29:30,360
Just shake your head first.

408
00:29:31,000 --> 00:29:32,080
Like this!

409
00:29:33,840 --> 00:29:36,080
- Again!
- Okay, okay, okay.

410
00:29:37,840 --> 00:29:39,440
Is it helping?

411
00:29:39,520 --> 00:29:40,560
I guess so.

412
00:29:41,080 --> 00:29:42,080
Shake it again.

413
00:29:42,160 --> 00:29:44,160
- How? How do I do it?
- Like this.

414
00:29:45,840 --> 00:29:47,760
- Like this?
- Good? Yeah.

415
00:29:47,840 --> 00:29:50,400
If you still don't feel better,
keep shaking.

416
00:29:50,480 --> 00:29:51,600
Just like this.

417
00:29:51,680 --> 00:29:53,320
Like this.

418
00:29:57,520 --> 00:29:58,800
Hurry up. Move some more.

419
00:29:58,880 --> 00:30:00,680
- Don't just laugh!
- Okay.

420
00:30:00,760 --> 00:30:03,520
Spin!

421
00:30:04,600 --> 00:30:07,640
Spin! And shake it all out!

422
00:30:11,200 --> 00:30:12,600
Junjai!

423
00:30:14,680 --> 00:30:16,880
Junjai! Are you okay?

424
00:30:22,520 --> 00:30:24,440
This way works the best.

425
00:30:25,240 --> 00:30:26,520
Come on, get in!

426
00:30:27,480 --> 00:30:28,800
Are you crazy?

427
00:30:28,880 --> 00:30:30,840
Come on. Jump in.

428
00:30:32,680 --> 00:30:34,720
Hurry up!

429
00:30:35,400 --> 00:30:37,720
Nobody's going to see you. Come on in.

430
00:30:38,360 --> 00:30:40,800
Jump in! Hurry up.

431
00:31:00,800 --> 00:31:02,360
Perfect.

432
00:31:03,440 --> 00:31:05,400
I'm not playing around anymore.

433
00:31:05,480 --> 00:31:08,800
One, two, three.

434
00:31:22,520 --> 00:31:26,920
Being like this kind of reminds me
of the day we first met.

435
00:31:28,760 --> 00:31:29,640
Right?

436
00:31:30,400 --> 00:31:34,080
Except you were
in way worse shape back then.

437
00:31:35,360 --> 00:31:36,200
Eh?

438
00:31:37,520 --> 00:31:38,640
But you're right.

439
00:31:41,800 --> 00:31:44,880
Then let me dry your hair this time.

440
00:31:44,960 --> 00:31:46,000
What? No need.

441
00:31:46,080 --> 00:31:47,920
- I can do it myself.
- Let me do it for you.

442
00:31:48,000 --> 00:31:50,320
Hey. Let me do it.

443
00:31:51,560 --> 00:31:54,320
Oops, your hair's in the way.

444
00:31:59,840 --> 00:32:03,560
Thank you for cheering me up today.

445
00:32:11,280 --> 00:32:14,240
I'm the one who should be thanking you.

446
00:32:16,360 --> 00:32:17,600
For everything.

447
00:32:21,600 --> 00:32:22,880
You're thanking me again?

448
00:32:25,560 --> 00:32:28,080
I really mean it, Aidao.

449
00:32:31,560 --> 00:32:38,400
At first, I didn't even think
I'd be able to stay at this school.

450
00:32:43,440 --> 00:32:46,320
And now my whole life's changed.

451
00:32:51,760 --> 00:32:53,560
It really feels like magic

452
00:32:54,720 --> 00:32:57,320
for someone ordinary like me.

453
00:33:00,920 --> 00:33:03,120
You make it sound like I'm not ordinary.

454
00:33:03,760 --> 00:33:07,520
I've got two arms and two legs,
just like you.

455
00:33:09,360 --> 00:33:10,200
That's not true.

456
00:33:11,040 --> 00:33:14,080
I think you're not ordinary.

457
00:33:15,560 --> 00:33:19,200
Or maybe you've got wings on your back.

458
00:33:19,280 --> 00:33:20,600
Let me see.

459
00:33:21,720 --> 00:33:24,320
- Do you really have two?
- Hey!

460
00:33:24,400 --> 00:33:26,000
- Let's see.
- No!

461
00:33:26,080 --> 00:33:27,920
Do you really have two wings?

462
00:33:28,000 --> 00:33:28,920
Hey.

463
00:33:39,160 --> 00:33:40,280
Seriously, though.

464
00:33:43,040 --> 00:33:45,320
You've brought me so far.

465
00:33:46,560 --> 00:33:47,840
I feel like

466
00:33:49,680 --> 00:33:53,040
I'm closer
to that wild little dream of mine…

467
00:33:54,840 --> 00:33:56,440
<i>than I've ever been.</i>

468
00:33:57,680 --> 00:33:58,920
You know what?

469
00:34:03,920 --> 00:34:05,280
What?

470
00:34:06,200 --> 00:34:09,440
I didn't even know you had a dream.

471
00:34:11,040 --> 00:34:12,440
I never told you.

472
00:34:13,920 --> 00:34:15,840
Well, tell me now.

473
00:34:16,600 --> 00:34:19,800
Promise you won't laugh first.

474
00:34:22,080 --> 00:34:23,440
Okay.

475
00:34:25,520 --> 00:34:28,920
This might sound a little dramatic,

476
00:34:29,880 --> 00:34:32,440
but when I sleep,

477
00:34:34,080 --> 00:34:37,360
I keep seeing
this strange image in my dreams.

478
00:34:40,400 --> 00:34:43,679
It's all jumbled up

479
00:34:45,560 --> 00:34:48,080
and hard to make sense of.

480
00:34:49,880 --> 00:34:51,320
It's blurry,

481
00:34:52,400 --> 00:34:55,080
but I can see all these lights.

482
00:34:55,760 --> 00:34:57,240
I can hear people clapping.

483
00:34:58,840 --> 00:35:05,200
And I can feel someone next to me.

484
00:35:07,400 --> 00:35:11,800
At first, I had no idea where it was.

485
00:35:13,120 --> 00:35:15,800
The whole thing felt
so far removed from my life.

486
00:35:18,240 --> 00:35:19,360
But you know what?

487
00:35:21,240 --> 00:35:23,640
That day at the modeling agency…

488
00:35:23,720 --> 00:35:25,320
Hey, watch out for the flash!

489
00:35:29,560 --> 00:35:32,000
<i>I suddenly felt like</i>

490
00:35:34,160 --> 00:35:35,680
<i>maybe</i>

491
00:35:36,800 --> 00:35:39,680
that dream was hiding in this industry.

492
00:35:44,360 --> 00:35:49,400
How amazing would it be
if I really became a model?

493
00:35:50,360 --> 00:35:52,880
<i>If I got to stand in the spotlight,</i>

494
00:35:53,880 --> 00:35:55,520
<i>be myself,</i>

495
00:35:57,160 --> 00:36:03,000
and find out who that person…

496
00:36:06,920 --> 00:36:09,720
Never mind. I'll stop there.

497
00:36:12,600 --> 00:36:13,520
Aidao?

498
00:36:15,200 --> 00:36:16,520
What's wrong?

499
00:36:17,800 --> 00:36:19,080
Are you okay?

500
00:36:20,000 --> 00:36:22,280
Aidao, say something.

501
00:36:22,360 --> 00:36:23,520
What's wrong?

502
00:36:27,040 --> 00:36:30,920
<i>Maybe it is a miracle.</i>

503
00:36:31,720 --> 00:36:33,680
<i>Or maybe it is just a coincidence.</i>

504
00:36:37,320 --> 00:36:42,240
<i>But to Aidao, it is fate.</i>

505
00:36:45,440 --> 00:36:52,000
<i>And that is enough for her</i>
<i>to make the biggest decision of her life.</i>

506
00:36:53,160 --> 00:36:54,320
You're sure about this?

507
00:36:55,320 --> 00:36:57,560
This is a pretty big way
to go against your dad.

508
00:36:59,320 --> 00:37:01,720
Yeah. I'm sure.

509
00:37:01,800 --> 00:37:02,920
Okay.

510
00:37:06,520 --> 00:37:07,640
Then let's do it.

511
00:38:09,240 --> 00:38:12,480
Guys, Toxxxxxin's IG is public now.

512
00:38:12,560 --> 00:38:14,440
No way! Let me see!

513
00:38:15,040 --> 00:38:16,800
It really is.

514
00:38:16,880 --> 00:38:18,560
Look.

515
00:38:19,480 --> 00:38:21,760
Hey, all five of them!

516
00:38:25,240 --> 00:38:26,880
Shit, what are they up to?

517
00:38:26,960 --> 00:38:28,400
Could it be…?

518
00:38:44,600 --> 00:38:46,000
Holy shit!

519
00:38:48,360 --> 00:38:50,960
HAS EVERYONE SEEN?
TOXXXXXIN'S RUNNING FOR STUDENT PRESIDENT!

520
00:38:54,120 --> 00:38:55,080
Holy shit!

521
00:38:55,160 --> 00:38:57,440
- NUMBER 3'S GOT THE CROWN ALREADY.
- WHO CAN EVEN COMPETE?

522
00:38:57,520 --> 00:38:59,360
WE ALREADY KNOW WHO'S WON
AND WE HAVEN'T EVEN VOTED

523
00:38:59,440 --> 00:39:00,920
NO. 3 IS WINNING BY A LANDSLIDE THIS YEAR!

524
00:39:01,000 --> 00:39:01,960
Don't worry, dude.

525
00:39:02,520 --> 00:39:05,200
The election's in less than two weeks.
They won't win.

526
00:39:15,400 --> 00:39:16,240
THERE SHE GOES AGAIN!

527
00:39:16,320 --> 00:39:17,480
<i>Number three, please.</i>

528
00:39:17,560 --> 00:39:19,440
Please vote number three.

529
00:39:27,000 --> 00:39:30,560
<i>As soon as sign-ups opened,</i>
<i>things took off like a whirlwind.</i>

530
00:39:31,440 --> 00:39:33,160
<i>But it was more than a passing trend.</i>

531
00:39:34,040 --> 00:39:39,760
<i>We all agreed that if we were doing this,</i>
<i>we wanted to make it count for our school.</i>

532
00:39:39,840 --> 00:39:43,480
<i>It had to help every student here,</i>
<i>including us.</i>

533
00:39:44,760 --> 00:39:47,840
<i>Hi! I'm here to share our policies.</i>

534
00:39:48,960 --> 00:39:53,000
<i>And everything we did to campaign</i>
<i>had to be sincere and make an impact.</i>

535
00:39:58,320 --> 00:40:01,240
And no student should ever…

536
00:40:01,320 --> 00:40:04,320
<i>Honestly, it was all so much fun.</i>

537
00:40:04,400 --> 00:40:05,760
<i>And it happened so fast.</i>

538
00:40:05,840 --> 00:40:07,080
- I LIKE THE IDEA. GLAM
- NUMBER 3

539
00:40:07,160 --> 00:40:08,000
<i>Superb.</i>

540
00:40:08,080 --> 00:40:09,640
THE TOXXXXXIN GIRLS ARE OUR HOPE.

541
00:40:10,960 --> 00:40:15,640
<i>Before we knew it, election day was here.</i>

542
00:40:15,720 --> 00:40:17,200
VOTING FORM

543
00:40:17,280 --> 00:40:19,480
<i>And of course, the winner was…</i>

544
00:40:19,560 --> 00:40:21,280
Your next student council president is

545
00:40:21,360 --> 00:40:25,240
candidate number three,
Aidao Laosathitphong!

546
00:40:25,320 --> 00:40:27,120
Yeah!

547
00:40:27,200 --> 00:40:30,160
Yeah! We did it.

548
00:40:30,240 --> 00:40:33,360
<i>Our mission was</i>
<i>on the home stretch.</i>

549
00:40:33,440 --> 00:40:36,040
LIST OF STUDENTS IN FAVOR
OF CHANGING THE RULE

550
00:40:38,280 --> 00:40:39,960
Adjust the section here.

551
00:40:40,040 --> 00:40:41,840
<i>And finally…</i>

552
00:40:49,120 --> 00:40:49,960
How'd it go?

553
00:40:51,680 --> 00:40:53,800
We got the rule changed!

554
00:40:56,160 --> 00:40:58,920
You are so good.

555
00:40:59,760 --> 00:41:05,160
<i>Who would've thought our crazy plan</i>
<i>would actually change everything?</i>

556
00:41:05,240 --> 00:41:08,760
TOXXXXXIN GIRLS CAN REALLY
CHANGE THE RULES, GUYS!!!

557
00:41:28,600 --> 00:41:29,720
All done.

558
00:41:31,080 --> 00:41:33,320
You girls really pulled it off.

559
00:41:33,400 --> 00:41:36,000
You know, every time
I talked to the school,

560
00:41:36,080 --> 00:41:38,280
they wouldn't budge.

561
00:41:38,360 --> 00:41:41,080
Junjai's management team is incredible.

562
00:41:42,200 --> 00:41:43,520
Of course we are.

563
00:41:44,480 --> 00:41:48,080
Take good care of Junjai from now on.

564
00:41:48,680 --> 00:41:51,280
Don't worry. We'll take good care of her.

565
00:41:53,080 --> 00:41:54,880
Maybe a little too good.

566
00:42:02,200 --> 00:42:03,800
Your false lash came off again?

567
00:42:04,720 --> 00:42:07,520
Didn't I tell you
not to rub your eyes so hard?

568
00:42:10,160 --> 00:42:11,000
Come here.

569
00:42:29,000 --> 00:42:30,000
I'm sorry.

570
00:42:30,880 --> 00:42:33,520
She's new to modeling.

571
00:42:35,520 --> 00:42:40,000
It's okay. I'm a rookie manager too.

572
00:42:41,400 --> 00:42:42,680
What are you looking at?

573
00:42:43,320 --> 00:42:44,160
Close your eyes.

574
00:43:30,200 --> 00:43:31,360
Hard to believe, huh?

575
00:43:38,120 --> 00:43:39,200
Congratulations.

576
00:44:13,680 --> 00:44:15,600
- Junjai?
- Huh?!

577
00:44:17,120 --> 00:44:22,080
Let's get you changed and
do the final touches on hair and makeup.

578
00:44:22,160 --> 00:44:23,000
Sure.

579
00:44:23,080 --> 00:44:25,240
Okay. I'll wait outside.

580
00:44:36,000 --> 00:44:37,720
Stand right there. Yeah, there.

581
00:44:39,320 --> 00:44:40,440
Gotcha.

582
00:44:40,520 --> 00:44:42,560
Must be hot in the dressing room, huh?

583
00:44:42,640 --> 00:44:44,320
Your face is bright red.

584
00:44:45,120 --> 00:44:46,200
Don't even start.

585
00:44:46,280 --> 00:44:47,960
"Don't even start."

586
00:44:52,040 --> 00:44:55,200
Oh, I haven't asked you yet.

587
00:44:55,280 --> 00:44:58,520
How did your family take the news about
you becoming student council president?

588
00:45:00,840 --> 00:45:01,920
My dad?

589
00:45:05,000 --> 00:45:06,320
He blew up, obviously.

590
00:45:07,680 --> 00:45:12,520
<i>Luckily, being student council president</i>
<i>still looks good for the family.</i>

591
00:45:12,600 --> 00:45:14,920
<i>Dim and Uncle Jess helped talk him around.</i>

592
00:45:15,560 --> 00:45:18,000
<i>Dad finally agreed.</i>

593
00:45:20,360 --> 00:45:24,880
But he'll definitely be watching me
more closely from now on.

594
00:45:25,480 --> 00:45:26,560
That sucks.

595
00:45:26,640 --> 00:45:29,880
So was it worth it? Everything we did?

596
00:45:29,960 --> 00:45:34,040
I guess only time will tell.

597
00:45:35,840 --> 00:45:37,240
Nobody knows yet.

598
00:45:41,200 --> 00:45:45,240
But even if we find out someday

599
00:45:45,320 --> 00:45:48,840
that we got nothing out of all this…

600
00:45:54,440 --> 00:45:56,120
I know I won't regret it.

601
00:46:03,440 --> 00:46:05,880
The model's here.

602
00:46:15,040 --> 00:46:16,160
Go on in.

603
00:46:16,240 --> 00:46:17,880
Go ahead, sweetie.
Stand right on this mark.

604
00:46:18,480 --> 00:46:20,600
Stunning. Let me see you turn around.

605
00:46:21,200 --> 00:46:22,120
You look gorgeous!

606
00:46:22,200 --> 00:46:23,840
How's the outfit? Does it fit okay?

607
00:46:27,040 --> 00:46:29,000
Let me try taking a few shots first.

608
00:47:12,160 --> 00:47:14,760
Hey, are you crying?

609
00:47:17,040 --> 00:47:18,040
Hey!

610
00:47:18,120 --> 00:47:20,040
What's wrong? Hey!

611
00:47:20,120 --> 00:47:21,160
- What?
- What?

612
00:47:21,240 --> 00:47:22,160
Shield her!

613
00:47:22,240 --> 00:47:24,280
- Why, though?!
- Don't know. Just do it!

614
00:47:24,360 --> 00:47:26,120
Oops.

615
00:47:26,200 --> 00:47:27,640
Why are you crying?

616
00:47:28,680 --> 00:47:30,600
What's that group so excited about?

617
00:47:31,880 --> 00:47:33,440
I was wondering the same thing.

618
00:47:34,040 --> 00:47:35,120
Forget it. Stay out of it.

619
00:47:35,200 --> 00:47:36,280
Hey?

620
00:47:38,000 --> 00:47:39,920
Junjai, what's wrong?

621
00:47:40,000 --> 00:47:40,840
Yes?

622
00:47:50,400 --> 00:47:52,280
What's wrong, Junjai? You're crying.

623
00:47:52,880 --> 00:47:54,480
Tissues!

624
00:47:54,560 --> 00:47:56,040
Tissues please.

625
00:47:56,120 --> 00:47:57,960
Quick, dab her face.

626
00:47:58,040 --> 00:48:00,160
What the hell is wrong with you?

627
00:48:03,760 --> 00:48:09,240
<i>That day, nobody knew</i>
<i>why Aidao and I were crying.</i>

628
00:48:10,720 --> 00:48:14,520
<i>Nobody could've guessed the photo</i>
<i>they happened to take right then</i>

629
00:48:15,600 --> 00:48:20,600
<i>would turn out so damn good</i>
<i>and end up everywhere.</i>

630
00:48:25,120 --> 00:48:26,720
<i>But I guess that's how life goes.</i>

631
00:48:29,720 --> 00:48:33,800
<i>It's never clear,</i>
<i>and you never know what's coming.</i>

632
00:48:34,480 --> 00:48:37,200
<i>One thing's for sure now, though.</i>

633
00:48:37,280 --> 00:48:42,680
<i>That scruffy girl from back then</i>
<i>had become a full-fledged model.</i>

634
00:48:46,720 --> 00:48:51,000
<i>It seemed like the first chapter</i>
<i>was coming to an end,</i>

635
00:48:51,760 --> 00:48:58,400
<i>just as the curtain was slowly rising</i>
<i>on the next one.</i>

636
00:49:00,200 --> 00:49:02,520
You sure you don't want a ride?

637
00:49:03,600 --> 00:49:06,800
Once you're famous,
I won't want you taking the bus anymore.

638
00:49:08,200 --> 00:49:09,920
It's dangerous.

639
00:49:10,000 --> 00:49:13,560
The agency's sending a car
to take me home today.

640
00:49:13,640 --> 00:49:15,320
Okay, then.

641
00:49:15,400 --> 00:49:17,120
Message us when you get home.

642
00:50:03,280 --> 00:50:04,600
You had a shoot today?

643
00:50:04,680 --> 00:50:06,640
You're really making a name for yourself.

644
00:50:09,440 --> 00:50:11,160
What have you got to show me this time?

645
00:50:31,880 --> 00:50:34,920
Uncle Jess, can I ask you something?

646
00:50:35,520 --> 00:50:36,520
What is it?

647
00:50:40,640 --> 00:50:42,720
Can I please stop doing this?

648
00:50:46,280 --> 00:50:48,360
I don't want to be a spy anymore.

649
00:51:17,360 --> 00:51:20,360
We'll need to pick up
the pace from here.

650
00:51:20,440 --> 00:51:24,360
So I'd like you all to come over to
my place this Saturday to prep.

651
00:51:24,440 --> 00:51:26,480
Get in the car, you hick!

652
00:51:26,560 --> 00:51:29,040
Who the hell's calling my niece a hick?

653
00:51:29,120 --> 00:51:33,560
Welcome to the Laosathitphong's manor.

654
00:51:33,640 --> 00:51:35,960
Shit, I'm lost.

655
00:51:36,520 --> 00:51:38,080
<i>What's up with you today?</i>

656
00:51:38,160 --> 00:51:39,440
<i>You've been pretty quiet.</i>

657
00:51:39,520 --> 00:51:41,600
Oh my goodness.

658
00:51:41,680 --> 00:51:43,840
There's something
I really need to confess to you.

659
00:51:45,560 --> 00:51:46,600
Can I…
